D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Tasks tab jump[/bold #D7AFFF]                                                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tasks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tasks: wire the Tasks pane task list onto the shared mixin.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]XPrompts tab jump[/bold #D7AFFF]                                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]xprompts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]xprompts: wire the XPrompt browser's non-header rows onto the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mixin and reserve the apostrophe in the filter-first browser input while[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the filter is empty.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Projects tab jump across all three sub-tabs[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]projects[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects: wire the projects list and the shared repo/workspace inventory[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pane base onto the shared mixin so each sub-tab jumps within its own [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Updates tab jump for Plugins and Agent CLIs[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]updates[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]updates: wire the Updates pane's active-sub-tab option list onto the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared mixin, skipping group headers and no-opping on the list-free Core[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sub-tab.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Config tab jump over visible tree rows[